 mix in the health care workforce: reviewing the evidence</article-title><source>Bull WHO</source><year>2002</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>575</fpage><lpage>580</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12163922</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Islam</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wakai</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Chowdhury</surname><given-names>AMR</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cost-effectiveness of community health workers in tuberculosis control in Bangladesh</article-title><source>Bull WHO</source><year>2002</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>445</fpage><lpage>450</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12132000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WHO Statistical Information System</collab></person-group><source>Human resource for health</source><publisher-name>Geneva, WHO</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/whosis/indicators/2007HumanResourcesForHealth/en/index.html"/><comment>Accessed 24 September 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Godinho</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Veen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dara</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cercone</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pacheco</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>Stopping TB in Central Asia: priorities for Action</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Washington DC, World Bank</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WHO</collab></person-group><source>African Health Monitor</source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><publisher-name>Brazzaville, WHO African Region, Congo</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.afro.who.int/press/periodicals/healthmonitor/jan-jun2007.pdf"/><comment>Accessed 23 September 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Global tuberculosis control: surveillance, financing</collab></person-group><source>WHO report 2005</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Geneva, World Health Organization</publisher-name><fpage>108</fpage><lpage>111</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/tb/publications/global_report/2005/annex1/en/index12.html"/><comment>Accessed 24 September 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Kaiser Family Foundation</collab></person-group><source>Global Health Facts</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.globalhealthfacts.org/index.jsp"/><comment>Accessed 24 September 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>Management of tuberculosis training for district TB coordinators</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Geneva, WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WHO</collab></person-group><article-title>WHO Global Tuberculosis Report, 2004. Nigeria</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/tb/publications/global_report/2004/en/Nigeria.pdf"/><comment>Accessed 24 September 2008</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2097487</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"